    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0352" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg246"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Coolidge to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Peking,
                                China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-05-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1888.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to department instruction No. 886
                    of March 2, 1905,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d231-f1"/> I have the honor to inclose a
                    copy of a memorandum which I communicated informally to the foreign office, with
                    regard to the position of the American Government as to the rights of real and
                    original owners of trade-marks.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Gardner Coolidge</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d231-a1.xml" xpointer="d231-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
